WEBVTT

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:39.740
Mine Fujiko!

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:44.200
Where am I?

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.460
Did some kind of human
experimentation take place here?

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.270
What is all this?

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.160
Fräulein Eule.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.190
Who's there?

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.010
Fräulein Eule.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.850
<i>"Fräulein Eule"?</i>

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:16.410
<i>Man, this looks like it's gonna be one twisted tale.</i>

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.310
<i>Now that I think about it, that nightmare</i>

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.110
<i>was only the beginning.</i>

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.040
Mine Fujiko?!

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.770
I would like you to steal Mine Fujiko.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.540
Oh dear, aren't <i>you</i> rude?

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.550
I'm afraid I must decline.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.180
I would like you to act on the calling card you sent

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.850
in a timely manner.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.850
<i>The calling card, huh?</i>

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.480
<i>It was back then...</i>

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.730
<i>To think we've been under their watch all along.</i>

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.650
<i>It isn't a passing fancy or desire.</i>

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.410
<i>She's the woman I want.</i>

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.080
<i>I don't care about the request.</i>

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:27.640
But I was informed that you take pride in unfailingly stealing that which you issue a calling card for.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.350
Go back to the forest,

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.080
Mr. Owl.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:40.210
Am I to take this as your refusal?

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.620
Man, I'm half awake. I gotta get to bed.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.820
Then I will excuse myself for tonight.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.280
See ya.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.740
<i>Owls are a pain in the ass.</i>

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.000
<i>They have sharp night vision.</i>

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.820
<i>But I need to know.</i>

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.660
<i>What do they want with Mine Fujiko?</i>

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.320
<i>What does she mean to them?</i>

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.650
Good to see you, Inspector Zenigata.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:21.010
Moving right along, I need transportation to the villa
owned by Count Almeida of the Glaucus Pharmaceuticals.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:22.690
Certainly, sir. However...

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.490
If we set out now, we'll arrive at a late hour.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.690
Let's save it for tomorrow—

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.490
I don't care.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.720
Bring me to the villa.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:31.700
Yes, sir.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.660
<i>This is supposed to be an international airport?</i>

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.990
<i>What a tiny country.</i>

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.720
Be grateful. I came all the way here to meet you,

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.720
Count Luis Yu Almeida.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.800
This is just an advance payment.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.730
Oh, that's a nice haul!

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.210
Fräulein Eule.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:14.090
It's a cult with a facility containing a narcotics production factory.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:14.790
From there—

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:15.540
A cult?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.250
Sorry, but I'm not getting involved in something shady like that.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.380
In that case, Lupin III,

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:27.630
just steal this woman who is sure to appear there.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.380
That is all we want from you.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.620
That's a fine woman.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.650
Another pain in the ass is here.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.300
You wait here.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.460
Yes, sir.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.380
I'll...

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.030
I assume Count Almeida is present.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.940
How may I help you?

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.660
I have some questions. Take me to him.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:05.920
Though you are policemen, do you not suppose you're intruding a bit late?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.990
It's still early evening. We're being
courteous enough by not forcing our way in.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.090
Oh?

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.050
And what exactly is this about?

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:18.470
Let us meet with the Count!

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.790
Do we need a search warrant after all?

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.130
Or is the renowned Count

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:27.630
ready to confess to his connection with dirty thieves?!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.240
What I have to ask concerns Lupin III.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:33.830
In that case,

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:35.740
I will take you to him.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.960
This place is full of owls, huh?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.720
Your master must be quite infatuated with them.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.640
Owls are servants of Minerva.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:49.900
She is known as the goddess
of wisdom that governs medicine.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.390
I see. How appropriate for a pharmaceutical company.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.320
This is the Count's bedroom.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.260
Thanks for leading me to him, Inspector.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:04.250
I know you've been in contact with Lupin III.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.380
What are you after?

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.770
The pharmaceutical company that you've supported

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.560
amassed a huge fortune using shady connections.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.030
Do the words "dizzy dizzy" mean anything to you?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:20.910
A cult which roped in believers using the influence
of a drug with that ridiculous name was destroyed.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.500
As luck would have it, Lupin was behind that.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.540
I wonder who his client was.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.840
I'm sure you know.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.100
<i>I see.</i>

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:34.030
<i>The pharmaceutics company was running that cult from behind to test the drug in humans.</i>

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.340
<i>It was a cover.</i>

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.860
The drug artificially overwrites personality.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:44.350
It was involved in the MKULTRA
experiments carried out by the CIA.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:50.610
Yes, it was behind the truth serums made from LSD and thiopental.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.110
Oh, scary.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:57.860
These so-called medical mafias kept
creating conspiracies over the Cold War.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.870
In other words, fear.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.670
Fear alone can control people.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.140
By controlling people through
making them doubt each other,

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.880
they could monopolize a vast fortune.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.140
I have a bone to pick with you for disturbing my sleep last time.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.180
Sorry to disturb you at night, old man.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.140
A mechanism?

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.600
How elaborate.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:33.940
Fräulein Eule.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:39.110
"The owl of Minerva spreads its wings only with the falling of the dusk."

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.190
Hegel?

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:41.910
Oh?

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:45.030
Then tell me when that butterfly will spread her wings,

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:46.630
Lupin III?

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.040
Who cares?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.540
When Hegel saw the Weltgeist in
Napoleon at the height of his career,

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:55.480
he sensed the demise of an age.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.920
I can still hear it even now.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:03.180
Minerva, the goddess of war that governs not only wisdom, but also justice...

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.390
I can hear her owl Glaucus flapping its wings.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.390
Fräulein Eule.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.880
Fräulein Eule.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.150
This is how the end will come

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.380
along with the dusk.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.660
I will ask you again.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.500
I would like you to steal Mine Fujiko,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.960
Lupin III.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.500
Straight ahead from here

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:38.370
is a town called Eulenspiegel.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.260
That place is in ruins and entry is forbidden.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:44.160
It doesn't matter. Just take us there.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.010
Yes, sir.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.520
Fräulein Eule, huh?

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:54.020
I had the narcotics crystal that
Lupin was after analyzed at a lab.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.520
When did you...

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:01.150
Preparation of purified drugs is not
something a cult can figure out alone.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:03.000
I knew there had to be someone behind it all.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:07.310
And they tried to contact Lupin once again.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.040
What are they after?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:14.040
The answer to that should be in the
abandoned Glaucus Pharmaceuticals buildings.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:33.350
<i>Fräulein Eule.</i>

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:36.560
Who are you?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:40.940
This isn't a place for the likes of you.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.360
And who are<i> you</i>?

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:45.930
I am Dr. Fritz Kaiser.

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.830
I was left behind in this town.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.880
A doctor, huh?

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.350
So, what is this place?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:55.510
The destroyed town whose name will be lost in the earth forever.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.730
This is Eulenspiegel.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:03.990
And here exists the Glaucus Pharmaceuticals
research facility, built to produce the fear of death.

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:09.290
They were secretly experimenting on people's minds here.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.710
There were Japanese scientist refugees here as well.

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:15.100
One of them was my wife.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:21.460
We extracted and crystallized a compound from a certain plant.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.360
A water-soluble hallucinogen.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:27.950
It caused a temporary euphoria.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:35.000
Acute poisoning induced assaultive behavior,
and some of them started perceiving humans as owls.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:36.960
Owls?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.270
Yes.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:40.790
When certain subjects took the drug,

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:43.380
they began shouting "Fräulein Eule."

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:46.380
They lost all their faculties shortly after,

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.970
and became permanently disabled.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.850
Fräulein Eule?

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.350
What does it mean?

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.770
In German, it means "Miss Owl."

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.760
Miss Owl, huh?

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:04.610
Anyway, why are you still here by yourself?

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:09.380
I'm searching for my daughter.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.870
By the name of...

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.370
Mine Fujiko.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.050
Congratulations.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:25.740
Hm?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.460
We don't have the results of the experiment yet.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.270
No, Professor.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.510
It's your birthday today, right?

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:32.300
Oh.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.390
Is it?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.820
We did have a party for your daughter on <i>her </i>birthday.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:43.700
I took my daughter's birthday away from her.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.730
And yet you're celebrating mine?

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.160
Professor...

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:56.940
A birthday party is a ceremony as meaningless as a
funeral that a person cannot attend because he's dead.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:01.030
There is no special difference
between life and death for people.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.790
Are you referring to <i>Memento mori</i>?

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:07.160
What's special is the fear that all life holds toward death.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:09.050
The fear in that process...

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.560
<i>A leak has been detected in Block C.</i>

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.550
<i>Block C will now be sealed off.</i>

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:15.050
Professor!

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:17.700
Professor, your mask!

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.520
Let's head to emergency exit!

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.480
I left the reagents in the lab!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.180
And my daughter is in the ward!

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.060
Professor!

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:26.770
I must find my daughter!

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.920
And that was the end of this place?

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.000
There was no news of it, even
though a whole town disappeared.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:42.660
Glaucus Pharmaceuticals didn't
care about exposing the truth.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.600
It was fear.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:47.170
It was to stage a cover-up of the situation.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:51.140
Yes, fear itself was my aspiration.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:54.260
But it slipped out of my grasp,

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:59.060
leaving me with eternal despair,

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.640
along with my daughter.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.200
Professor?

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.640
Mine Fujiko?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.290
A town erased from memory.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:24.950
The cause was an accident thirteen years ago.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:30.200
They took only the reagents
that hadn't been clinically tested

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.540
and closed this research facility.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.150
Thirteen years ago...

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:37.440
It coincides with the time that cult rose to prominence.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:42.770
The cult of Fräulein Eule was a convenient
experimentation ground for Glaucus Pharmaceuticals.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.780
But that alone wouldn't motivate Lupin.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.830
Inspector, you've known all this from the beginning?

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:50.480
But you didn't—

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.760
...tell you anything, right?

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.030
Who do you think you are?

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:58.020
Am I your subordinate?

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.390
No, of course not.

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:02.030
Don't get in my way anymore.

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:05.090
You're free to follow me from now on, but...

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.920
look here, this is <i>my</i> case.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:11.720
Inspector.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.130
To go this far...

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:21.390
Professor, where are you?

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.390
So you came, Lupin.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:31.910
I was just thinking the same thing about you.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.460
When I try to have some fun with the "dizzy dizzy" drug,

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.910
and things start getting good, you show up.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.290
Don't play dumb, Lupin.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:46.450
You're after neither the cult's narcotics nor the great fortune that you could make off it.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.230
What do you mean?

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:49.920
It's Mine Fujiko.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:55.760
You're after the woman created in the human experimentation here.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:59.880
The unshakable proof of the evil deed that links the cult and the pharmaceutical company!

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:02.430
Sorry to interrupt you in the middle of your speech,

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.960
but there's shaking proof right behind you.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:15.150
Hey, Lupin!

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.390
Who are these guys?

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.650
Illusions!

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.060
They were whipped up by Fräulein Eule!

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:23.710
If they're really illusions, we shouldn't have to worry about being shot.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.000
Wanna put that to the test?

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.930
You're the one they're after!

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.830
You also know too much.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.750
The secret about the Count's precious treasure.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.390
We're outnumbered.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.460
You got that right!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:39.470
Professor!

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.200
What are you doing here?

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:44.850
What's going on?!

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:45.930
Hey!

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.920
<i>Just how much of this is an illusion?</i>

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.510
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:06.490
Hey, you!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:07.990
Come this way!

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.250
Hurry and come!

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:13.640
Where are we?

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:17.280
A part of my story,
and at the same time, the entirety of it.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:22.860
Hey...

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.570
You experimented on your own daughter, didn't you?

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.010
I had believed...

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:32.140
that experiment would put an end to long, brutal strife.

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:36.520
That's why I offered up my beloved daughter. However...

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:40.090
...you were buried here along with the entire city

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:42.750
and lost both your research and your daughter.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.920
So why did you save me?

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.960
I want you to save...

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.110
my daughter.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.330
It's a new morning!

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.040
Not like the evening!

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.270
You're special!

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:59.260
And if I'm so special,

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.820
what day is it for me?

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:04.520
Happy birthday!

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.050
Professor?

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.810
He's not here anymore.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.520
This is my story, after all.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:14.720
Not quite.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.990
This is because of Fräulein Eule.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.060
I'll be back to normal when I wake up.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:20.520
I'm not so sure.

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:25.860
There are people who lose sight of the exit and get stuck in a story all their life.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:26.840
Like the professor?

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:27.780
Yup.

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:30.160
How do I find the exit?

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:34.600
Make use of something linked to reality to catch me.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.700
For instance, pain!

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:39.880
Why must I catch you?

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.090
Weren't you listening?

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:44.090
It's because this is <i>my</i> story.

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:44.970
Damn it.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.570
Guess I'll play along.

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.220
This way!

00:18:58.690 --> 00:18:59.480
Too bad!

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:00.980
Over here!

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:09.160
<i>What am I chasing after?</i>

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:10.410
<i>An illusion?</i>

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:12.120
<i>Mine Fujiko?</i>

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:13.910
<i>That's it.</i>

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:14.850
<i>Fujiko.</i>

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:17.980
Ouch!

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.680
Enough of that.

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:21.920
Huh? You're giving up?

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.660
You're gonna disappear, too, right?

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:25.010
Do whatever you want.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.260
Are you sure?

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:28.510
Yeah, go ahead.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.050
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.460
Gotcha!

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.770
Don't be so rough, Lupin.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:53.440
Fräulein Eule... Fräulein Eule...

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.800
What a wonderful twilight.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.830
Perfect time to meet one's demise.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.820
Professor.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.040
You're an illusion.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.840
You're dead.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.490
It's all just a story.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:10.000
A story cannot bring salvation.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.190
However, Lupin III...

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:16.720
The moment you lay your hand on it,
butterflies will soar and everything will collapse.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.730
Inspector Zenigata!

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:24.550
Please get a hold of yourself!

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:32.400
Glaucus Pharmaceuticals covered up the accident by wiping out the city.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:35.740
Furthermore, they carried out human experimentation.

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:40.710
The child of Dr. Fritz Kaiser, who he called "Daughter,"

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:44.250
was a test subject as well, according to a disturbing rumor.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.180
Hey, stop it.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.750
Eulenspiegel is still private property.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.510
Are you going to bring charges with
evidence gathered from trespassing?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.400
And what happened to Lupin?

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:59.800
The pharmaceutical company's president, Luis Yu Almeida and Lupin are both after that woman!

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.520
Lupin will show up there for sure.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.270
Mine Fujiko!

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.530
This is...

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:14.130
That wasn't a dream.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:15.960
But is it the truth?

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.980
Fräulein Eule.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.410
<i>Was this nightmare...</i>

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:26.120
<i>just the story of a woman named Mine Fujiko?</i>
